# Kanban Tracking Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Kanban tracking. Detail: `docs/agent-workflows/kanban-tracking.md`.

Cards: `.devtool/features/*.md` (`status` = workflow phase id). Columns: `.devtool/README.md`.

## Hard rule

**Every task/chat needs a card** — read-only, Tiny, Normal, High-risk, ops/recovery, architecture review, Q&A. No exceptions.

| Mode | Card |
|------|------|
| All | **required** — create at session start if none linked |

## Session start

1. Find linked card (user `@` path, same title, or active WIP in `align`…`verify`/`blocked`).
2. No card → **create** under `.devtool/features/` (do not skip; do not wait for user ask).
3. Set `status` to current phase; append **Progress** note: date, chat scope, next step.

## During work

- **One feature thread = one card** — append **Progress** per slice/sub-step; do not spawn sibling cards (`-r2`, `-step2`) for the same epic.
- Sub-step done → tick Acceptance + Progress; stay in `implement`/`verify` until full Acceptance met.
- Phase change → move `status` + append Progress (what changed, evidence).
- `BLOCKED:` → `status: blocked` + blocker note.
- **Full** scope complete (all required Acceptance) → `verify` then `done`; archive per extension. Optional/deferred steps: note in Progress, do not early-archive.

Update card **before** claiming done — not only in chat summary.

## Pivot / skip / new task (mandatory warning)

Before unrelated work when a WIP card exists (`status` not `done` or `backlog`):

```text
LEFTOVER_WIP:
- card: <id or path>
- status: <phase>
- unfinished: <acceptance / steps left>
- to park: move to blocked/backlog + note, or finish first
```

Do not silently abandon. User must **explicitly** park (`blocked`/`backlog` + reason) or finish.

## Card body (minimum)

Under title: **Scope**, **Acceptance**, **Artifacts** (when architecture thread — link `docs/architecture/<slug>/`), **Progress** (timestamped bullets). Keep frontmatter `modified` accurate.
